From: jaejinaa <wowls7990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:24:51 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(gitlab): connect a self-hosted GitLab

A connection for a self-hosted GitLab: its base URL and a personal, project or group access token, stored in the connection's existing columns and envelope-encrypted secret. The catalog entry carries only the git scopes (git.read, git.write) and is not listed in the web catalog yet, because the API-key form has no base-URL field: an admin creates it through POST /organizations/{orgId}/connectors with serverUrl and apiKey. git/gitlab.ts holds the base URL/API derivation, the git and REST headers and the merge-base call the proxy uses.
